[
  {
    "id": "sitl20-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 20 Move stream stop",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "ArduPilot SITL move stream proof: prepare with Arm + GUIDED, stream a forward local velocity setpoint, then stop by injecting zero velocity (replaces/stops the prior stream). Do not use payload:false \u2014 that is the toolkit-wide suppress rule and never reaches stream.stop().",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl20-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl20-tab",
    "name": "Move stream with explicit stop",
    "info": "Adapted from examples/23-velocity-joystick.json for the SITL lab. Connection binds 0.0.0.0:14550 and sends to 127.0.0.1:14551.\n\nUse the Arm + GUIDED inject first. Then fire Fwd 1 m/s to start the stream. The Stop inject sends velocity {north:0,east:0,up:0}; mavlink-move stops the prior stream before starting the zero-velocity stream (DESIGN.md: payload===false suppresses and must not be used as stop).",
    "x": 230,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
